se when it did not. Scripts calling the greeter branch on it.\n  - term: standard output\n    means: >-\n      The lines the command prints for its user, its answer and its log\n      records alike. It is the greeter's only visible output.\n\ncatalogue:\n  - template: 'the greeting is configured as \"{greeting}\"'\n    block: given\n    means: >-\n      The project's config file sets the greeting, the word the greeter\n      prints before a name, to the quoted text.\n    terms: [greeting]\n  - template: 'the {actor:role} runs \"{command}\"'\n    block: when\n    means: >-\n      That role runs the quoted command line once, in the project\n      directory, and waits for it to exit.\n    terms: [command]\n  - template: 'the command exits with code {code:number}'\n    block: then\n    means: >-\n      The command that role ran ended with that exit code; 0 means it\n      succeeded.\n    terms: [command, exit code]\n  - template: 'stdout matches {expected:pattern}'\n    block: then\n    means: >-\n      A line the command printed to its standard output matches the\n      pattern, a regular expression: either the answer line the command\n      prints for its user, or a log record's message or fields.\n    terms: [command, standard output]\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
